THIRD-PARTY DATA: Australian Government Information Security Manual (ISM)
================================================================================

This repository vendors and redistributes control catalogue data from the
Australian Government Information Security Manual (ISM), published in Open
Security Controls Assessment Language (OSCAL) format by the Australian Signals
Directorate (ASD) / Australian Cyber Security Centre (ACSC).

  Title      : Information security manual (ISM), OSCAL release
  Author     : Australian Signals Directorate, Commonwealth of Australia
  Source     : https://www.cyber.gov.au/ism/oscal
  Mirror     : https://github.com/AustralianCyberSecurityCentre/ism-oscal
  Copyright  : (C) Commonwealth of Australia
  Licence    : Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
               https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Vendored copies live under `oscal/upstream/ism/<release-tag>/` and record the
exact upstream git tag and SHA-256 checksum of every file.

CHANGES MADE TO THE LICENSED MATERIAL
-------------------------------------
CC BY 4.0 requires that modifications be indicated. This project:

  * Redistributes the ISM OSCAL catalogue and profile documents BYTE-FOR-BYTE
    UNMODIFIED under `oscal/upstream/`. No ISM control text is altered.
  * Produces SEPARATE derived artefacts (OSCAL profiles, component-definitions,
    crosswalk mappings and assessment results) that REFERENCE ISM control
    identifiers. These derived artefacts are the work of this project and are
    NOT part of the licensed ISM material.

Derived artefacts and any interpretation of ISM controls expressed in this
repository are NOT endorsed by, affiliated with, or approved by the Australian
Signals Directorate, the Australian Cyber Security Centre, or the Commonwealth
of Australia. Where this repository's interpretation of a control differs from
the ISM, THE ISM IS AUTHORITATIVE.

The Commonwealth Coat of Arms and the ASD logo are excluded from the CC BY 4.0
licence and are NOT reproduced in this repository.
  https://www.pmc.gov.au/government/commonwealth-coat-arms

