THIRD-PARTY DATA: operating-system end-of-life dates
================================================================================

  Title   : endoflife.date product lifecycle data
  Author  : endoflife.date contributors
  Source  : https://endoflife.date
  Licence : MIT

Vendored under `data/eol/`, normalised and checksummed.

IMPORTANT: this data is COMMUNITY-MAINTAINED and is NOT vendor-authoritative.
For a compliance assertion about vendor support, the vendor's own lifecycle
documentation is the authority. Checks consuming this data therefore report
`proxy` confidence and never `direct`, and a deployment may override entries
with vendor-confirmed dates.

================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CONTENT: ansible-lockdown (reference only)
================================================================================

  Author  : MindPoint Group - A Tyto Athene Company / Ansible Lockdown
  Source  : https://github.com/ansible-lockdown
  Licence : MIT

No ansible-lockdown code is vendored or executed by this project. Their STIG
and CIS roles are remediation content and would modify a host, which is
incompatible with this project's read-only assessment guarantee; see
docs/adr/0012-mine-ansible-lockdown-tags-do-not-execute-its-roles.md.

Their task TAGS (STIG rule, Vuln ID, CCI and NIST 800-53 identifiers) are used
as one input when authoring control crosswalks, attributed under MIT.

